<title>BELGIUM: Socialist MEPs slam Renault &quot;arrogance&quot;.</title>
<headline>Socialist MEPs slam Renault &quot;arrogance&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Socialist members of the European Parliament on Thursday accused French car maker Renault of &quot;arrogance and disdain&quot; in its handling of the closure of a Belgian assembly plant.</p>
<p>A group of European Socialist Party MEPs tabled a motion condemming Renault following a visit to the plant at Vilvoorde, north of Brussels.</p>
<p>Group leader Pauline Green said in a statement that representatives of the factory workforce had been invited to Strasbourg next week to speak to a full session of the parliament.</p>
<p>Renault last weekend stunned workers and Belgian authorities when it announced the closure of the profitable factory as part of a plan to cut costs.</p>
<p>Although popular with shareholders, the decision has met with widespread criticism and the European Commission has said the company clearly ignored legally binding EU directives on the procedure.</p>
</text>
